From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 13:49:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] test(int): draw services.int.test days from the future,
 not from a fixed 2024 base

The helper day() returned 20_000 + rand(20_000) days since 1970. Day 20_000 is 2024-10-04, so draws before today (about 4% on 2026-11-01)
made the trip state machine refuse the schedule with 'trip already departed' (23514). Base the draw on today + 30 days.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01N5EMQFD9tczZMCXDkiPAsC
---
 tests/integration/services.int.test.ts | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tests/integration/services.int.test.ts b/tests/integration/services.int.test.ts
index b07f1d8..c258cf7 100644
--- a/tests/integration/services.int.test.ts
+++ b/tests/integration/services.int.test.ts
@@ -24,7 +24,10 @@ async function fails(p: Promise<unknown>): Promise<AppError> {
   }
   throw new Error('expected the call to fail');
 }
-const day = () => 20_000 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 20_000); // random far-future day => re-runnable
+// Random day number (days since 1970) in [today + 30, today + 30 + 20_000): always in the future (the trip state machine refuses
+// past departures) and still random enough to be re-runnable. The old fixed base 20_000 is 2024-10-04, so ~4% of draws were past.
+const TODAY = Math.floor(Date.now() / 86_400_000);
+const day = () => TODAY + 30 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 20_000);
 const at = (d: number, h: number) => new Date(Date.UTC(1970, 0, 1 + d, h)).toISOString();
 
 describe.skipIf(!URL_)('Phase 4 services against real Postgres + PostgREST + RLS', () => {
